            {
              "number": 22,
              "text": "Maya says a mistaken belief about theatre programmes is that",
              "options": [
                {
                  "value": "A",
                  "label": "Theatres pay companies to produce them"
                },
                {
                  "value": "B",
                  "label": "Few theatre-goers buy them nowadays"
                },
                {
                  "value": "C",
                  "label": "They contain far more adverts than previously"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "number": 23,
              "text": "Finn was surprised that, in early Brit ish theatre, programmes",
              "options": [
                {
                  "value": "A",
                  "label": "were difficult for audiences to obtain"
                },
                {
                  "value": "B",
                  "label": "were given out free of charge"
                },
                {
                  "value": "C",
                  "label": "were seen as a kind of contract"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "number": 24,
              "text": "Maya feels their project should include an explanation of why companies of actors",
              "options": [
                {
                  "value": "A",
                  "label": "promoted their own plays"
                },
                {
                  "value": "B",
                  "label": "performed plays outdoors"
                },
